    rdfs:label "Evidence for Canes Rattans not Ground used in Hat-Making, Brushes, Upholstery & Turnery: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 326"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "RATTANS: a commercial name for the long trailing stems of the Calamus Royleanus and Roxburghii, and various other species of palms, which form a considerable article of import from India and the Eastern archipelago. They are extensively used, when split, for caulking chairs, and for making rough brooms, and, when dyed black as a substitute for whalebone for ..."@en ;
